{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784312521,"nonce":"5Fll5Nu5MEApR+1Xb5LuMigaQAs=","title":"[dogfood] scarab-server Pod has read-only /tmp — downstream step launch EROFS-poisons the run (dead-letter)","message":"With readOnlyRootFilesystem:true (deploy/helm/scarab/values.yaml), the server Pod only mounted a writable emptyDir at /home/scarab/.scarab. But the k8s executor stages workspace CAS tarballs through tempfile::tempdir() (respects TMPDIR, defaults to /tmp) when launching a step that needs a prior step's workspace — crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs:332/371/450. /tmp was on the read-only root FS, so materializing the checkout workspace for the 'check' step failed: 'workspace: Read-only file system (os error 30) at path /tmp/.tmpXXXX'.\n\nThe launch_step outbox intent retried to MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS (10) and was dead-lettered as poison (scheduler.rs:707-719); the whole run transitioned Running-\u003eDeadLettered with checkout (which had already cloned successfully, exit 0) cancelled. Distinct from 9cdf38e (that was the step Pod's /tmp / settle, PR #22) — this is the SERVER Pod's /tmp.\n\nSymptom is near-silent: only a benign 'cas gc pass failed / object not found' WARN; the real reason lives in the RunDeadLettered event payload.\n\nFix (committed): mount a writable emptyDir at /tmp in the server Deployment (mirrors the step-Pod /tmp fix).","files":null}]}